  "body": "Stacked on #4022. Own commit range: `028530986..bea85a429` (one commit). Retarget this PR to `main` before #4022 merges.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- A Wire Contour with the side **Die** on one selected closed DXF chain now posts through the Agie Wire EDM (AgieVision) post. Before this change, the post refused it (\"reads a selected DXF chain only for a captured punch\").\n- The ISO keeps the nominal walls. It starts at the seam and runs counter-clockwise, with `G01`, `G02` and `G03` blocks and incremental `I`/`J` centres. A clockwise drawing is reversed.\n- The SBL and SBR are the zero-step die setup of #2957 (`c_die`). Only the stem, the stock and the hole change.\n- The control makes the lead, the passes and the separation. CamCraft writes no lead.\n- The app reads the placed walls with the code of the inspection export (#3219). That code is now shared in `crates/app/src/operation/agie_opening.rs`. The inspection export keeps its behaviour.\n- The ordinary Wire Contour generator and the wire laws still judge the generated kerf before the native post runs.\n- New: `crates/post/src/agie/opening.rs`, `crates/post/src/agie/opening/walls.rs` (exact distances between lines and arcs), `examples/agie/reentrant-die.{dxf,camscript}`, a user guide section and `docs/decisions/3178-agie-reentrant-opening.md`.\n\n## Rules and refusals\n\nEach rule uses the rough offset of the 20 mm QN2 row (0.245 mm). Each refusal names the rule and its values.\n\n| Rule | Refusal starts with | Control evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Joints and arc centres on the 0.00001 mm grid, equal squared radii at both arc ends | `Native arc radius rule` (both radii) | `RADB` (0.001 mm difference): the control moved the centre by half the difference. `RADA` (0.003 mm): no plotted path, no message. |\n| An inside fillet of the plate (a CCW arc of the CCW opening) has a radius larger than 0.245 mm | `Native arc offset rule` (radius, offset) | `FILR` (R0.2): FORMALCHECK passed, but the Main pass left the arc out and cut a sharp corner. The control does not refuse it. CamCraft refuses it. |\n| An arc joins its neighbours tangentially; only two straight walls meet at a sharp corner | `Native joint rule` (the point) | `REENT20`: the sharp tooth tips got round R0.245 turns. |\n| A sharp inside corner of the plate leaves at most 0.002 mm | `Strict cover rule` (angle, rest) | Same law as the polygon die. |\n| Walls that are not neighbours are more than 2 × (corner reach + 0.245) apart | `The walls from … are … mm apart` | Conservative bound. |\n| Hole inside, more than 1 mm from each wall; straight entry wall parallel to X or Y; 3 mm lead and 3 mm of wall each side; lead 0.4 mm clear of other walls | hole and entry texts | `REENT20`: straight lead from the hole to the seam. |\n| 0.4 mm of stock beyond each wall and arc extremum; 20 mm plate | stock texts | Same as the polygon die. |\n\n\"Tangent entry radius larger than the offset\" does not apply: CamCraft writes no arc lead.\n\n## Imported on an offline copy of the control's software (2026-11-25)\n\n- `REENT20` (unmodified output of `examples/agie/reentrant-die.camscript`):\n  - The ISO and SBL arrived byte for byte. The tree showed `CCB030[0]`.\n  - One formal error before TECCUT (\"Technologie : te definiëren\"). TECCUT row 0199 (Dia 0.25, H20, Ra 0.30) was assigned. The tree showed `CCB030[4]`, offsets 245, 155, 140 and 134 µm.\n  - FORMALCHECK: no errors. Only the two usual warnings.\n  - Plot: the Main pass runs counter-clockwise 0.245 mm inside the opening. The fillets became concentric arcs of r − 0.245. The clockwise R4 tongue tip became a concentric `G02` of R4.245. The Main pass ends 1 mm before the seam. The trims run reversed.\n- `FILR`, `RADA` and `RADB` are the same job with one hand edit of the ISO each. CamCraft refuses those edits.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/agie-native/REENT20.ISO`, line by line in `opening_tests.rs`. N0001 is the seam (the foot of the 5 mm lead from X0 Y−7). N0003 is the R2 corner. N0005 and N0009 are the tooth fillets. N0006 to N0008 are the tooth. N0013 and N0017 are the tongue fillets. N0015 is the R4 tongue tip (G02 about X0 Y4). N0022 returns to the seam.\n- The CAM path of the example: 25 moves, the wire laws clean, one captured slug of 789.12 mm².\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` lib, `agie::opening_tests` (9 tests): the golden ISO, the clockwise drawing, the entry choice, each refusal with its values.\n- `camcraft-app --test agie_native`:\n  - `opening::a_reentrant_line_and_arc_die_posts_g02_g03_and_the_checked_die_setup` (ISO golden, SBL = DIE20 with the stem, stock and hole changed, SBR).\n  - `opening::a_small_concave_arc_an_island_or_an_outside_hole_publishes_nothing`.\n- `camcraft-app --test wire_dxf_selection`: `arcs::a_reentrant_die_of_lines_and_arcs_passes_the_laws_and_a_2um_gouge_does_not`. The laws accept the generated cut. A 2 µm move of the tongue tip arc into the plate gives a `Gouge`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. One golden is new: `REENT20.ISO`. The straight-only and arc punch Agie goldens are byte-identical (the whole `agie_native` suite and the post lib `agie::` tests pass).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A physical machine and the slug restraint.\n- An off-grid DXF (refused), sharp joints at an arc (refused), conical arcs and other heights than 20 mm.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on the head `bea85a429`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: the diff of #4022 touches `crates/geometry`, so quick fell back to the batch plan. 1215 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 48.1 min. This includes `agie_native`, `wire_dxf_selection`, `wire_post`, `sodick_wire_post`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `post suites: script_agie_native`, the post lib, the ui suites and `clippy -D warnings`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Strict clippy `-p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- P6: no heavy step.\n\nChangelog: The Agie Wire EDM (AgieVision) post writes a selected die opening from a DXF chain of lines and arcs, also a reentrant one, with native G01/G02/G03 and the zero-step die setup; arcs that the control would change are refused by name.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3178\n\n",
